_fcec135b_003","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"application","question":"If $f(x) = x^2$ and $g(y) = \\sin y$, what is $(g\\circ f)'(x)$?","options":["$\\sin(2x)$","$x^2\\cos x$","$2\\sin(x^2)$","$2x\\cos(x^2)$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"a41f6591a81e34653f73a865"},{"id":"year_1_1a_math_i_calculus_chain_rule_fcec135b_004","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"application","question":"If $f(x) = \\mathrm{e}^x$ and $g(y) = y^3$, what is $(g\\circ f)'(x)$?","options":["$3\\mathrm{e}^{x}$","$\\mathrm{e}^{3x}$","$x^3\\mathrm{e}^{x}$","$3\\mathrm{e}^{3x}$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"a3f4e519d4125fa4c31b12d1"},{"id":"year_1_1a_math_i_calculus_chain_rule_fcec135b_005","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"conceptual","question":"Which differentiability condition is enough to apply the chain-rule setup?","options":["The composition is differentiable only when both functions are linear.","The composition of differentiable functions is differentiable.","Differentiability of the outer function alone is enough.","The derivative of a composition is always the product of the two original functions."],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"d3dd805ffa19660de9dba3ef"},{"id":"year_1_1a_math_i_calculus_chain_rule_fcec135b_006","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"conceptual","question":"Which formula matches the chain rule in the proposition?","options":["$(g\\circ f)'(x) = g'(f(x))f'(x)$","$(g\\circ f)'(x) = g'(x)+f'(x)$","$(g\\circ f)'(x) = g(f'(x))$","$(g\\circ f)'(x) = f'(g(x))g'(x)$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"78b20a8803f26c245d98b48c"},{"id":"year_1_1a_math_i_calculus_chain_rule_fcec135b_007","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"application","question":"Let $f(x) = x+1$ and $g(y) = 2y$. What is $(g\\circ f)'(x)$?","options":["$2$","$2x+2$","$1$","$x+1$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"5ec9586a06635b081669d541"},{"id":"year_1_1a_math_i_calculus_chain_rule_fcec135b_008","difficulty":"standard","